{
  "decision": "D482 (owner 2026-11-28; narrows D395/D396/D404): most PRs are reviewed by the GitHub GLM reviewer and its exact-head verdict counts. A Codex/GPT Sol-tier verdict is required ONLY for an IMPORTANT PR: (a) privacy, consent, credentials, tokens or security; (b) merge gates, the gate and reviewer workflows (every workflow that triggers, labels, dispatches or posts reviews or gate inputs: merge-gates*, pr-review*, review-label, mac-compile*, trusted-mac, data-sync, post-merge-hosted), release/packaging/signing/notarization workflows, shared actions, release and signing (a feature PR that only adds a test leg to ci.yml or desktop.yml is NORMAL); (c) an owner-reported fix PR (its body has a Ledger: G3-nn line, rule R13; its tier is at least ledgerMinTier, so even a docs-only one needs the verdict). A PR is IMPORTANT when it carries a label below, its body matches ledger, a trusted REVIEW-TIER: <overrideTier> comment raises it, it touches maxFiles or more files, a file is renamed, it has no file list, or ANY touched non-test path matches ANY area pattern (one important path makes the whole PR important; test files, rules.mjs TEST_RE, never match an area). An IMPORTANT PR is at least tier importantMinTier, so a workflow-only or docs-only IMPORTANT PR (path tier 0) still needs the Sol verdict. Path tier 2, spanning native Swift and cockpit web, and design-touching no longer make a PR important by themselves. On an IMPORTANT PR (ghglm) never decides (REVIEW_GLM_TIERS does not widen it); Terra decides only tier 1 of a NORMAL PR. Patterns are case-insensitive (ledger is also multi-line) and use only syntax JavaScript and Python read alike. The coordinator (decide.py review_class) reads this same file from main; both sides test against examples.",
  "version": 2,
  "maxFiles": 100,
  "labels": ["review:codex", "review:gpt"],
  "ledger": "^[ \\t>*-]*Ledger:.*\\bG3-[0-9]+",
  "overrideTier": 2,
  "ledgerMinTier": 1,
  "importantMinTier": 1,
  "areas": [
    { "area": "consent", "re": "consent|scope_policy|(^|/)scopes?\\.go$|erase_scope|forget_identity" },
    { "area": "privacy", "re": "privacy|redact|^cli/internal/diagnostics/|(^|/)Diagnostics[A-Za-z]*\\.swift$" },
    { "area": "credentials", "re": "credential|keychain|secret|manualkey|identity|_login\\.go$|LoginService|claudesession|browser_session|oauth|(auth|access|refresh|bearer|api|session)[_-]?token|api[_-]?key" },
    { "area": "security", "re": "sandbox|entitlement|permission|(^|/)SECURITY|-pin[^/]*$|(^|/)pins?\\.[a-z]+$|(^|/)go\\.(mod|sum)$|(^|/)Package\\.resolved$|(^|/)package-lock\\.json$" },
    { "area": "gates-ci", "re": "^\\.github/workflows/(merge-gates|pr-review|review-label|mac-compile|trusted-mac|data-sync|post-merge-hosted)[^/]*$|^\\.github/workflows/[^/]*(release|packag|candidate|sign|notar|distribution)[^/]*$|^\\.github/actions/|^scripts/(merge-gates|pr-review|mac-compile)/|^desktop/native/verification/scenario-tiers\\.tsv$" },
    { "area": "release", "re": "release|notari[sz]|codesign|signing|sparkle|cliupdate|(^|/)update\\.go$|install|\\.entitlements$|(^|/)Info\\.plist$" }
  ],
